      <Prose>For a written route, Richard Weber's Markov notes work from finite chains through hitting times and long-run behavior. Read their first-passage equations beside the reserve example. Karl Sigman's Brownian notes give a compact path from random-walk motivation to covariance, martingales and barriers. Pair these with the worked objects on this page: transition rows and first-step systems for chains, then shared increments and reflected endpoints for Brownian motion.</Prose>
